      "label": "hoverResult",
      "result": {
        "contents": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "\n```rust\ncore\n```\n\n```rust\npub mod cmp\n```\n\n---\n\nUtilities for comparing and ordering values.\n\nThis module contains various tools for comparing and ordering values. In\nsummary:\n\n* [`PartialEq<Rhs>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html) overloads the `==` and `!=` operators. In cases where\n  `Rhs` (the right hand side's type) is `Self`, this trait corresponds to a\n  partial equivalence relation.\n* [`Eq`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.Eq.html) indicates that the overloaded `==` operator corresponds to an\n  equivalence relation.\n* [`Ord`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.Ord.html) and [`PartialOrd`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.PartialOrd.html) are traits that allow you to define total and\n  partial orderings between values, respectively. Implementing them overloads\n  the `<`, `<=`, `>`, and `>=` operators.\n* [`Ordering`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/enum.Ordering.html) is an enum returned by the main functions of [`Ord`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.Ord.html) and\n  [`PartialOrd`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.PartialOrd.html), and describes an ordering of two values (less, equal, or\n  greater).\n* [`Reverse`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/struct.Reverse.html) is a struct that allows you to easily reverse an ordering.\n* [`max`] and [`min`] are functions that build off of [`Ord`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.Ord.html) and allow you\n  to find the maximum or minimum of two values.\n\nFor more details, see the respective documentation of each item in the list.\n\n[`max`]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.Ord.html#method.max\n[`min`]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.Ord.html#method.min"
        }
      }
    },
